be strengthened and enlivened and renewed from the power of the holy Shabbos; in such a manner that I never fall into sadness or depression at all throughout all the days of the week — because of the abundance of the strength of the joy and exultation of the holy Shabbos.
יְהִי רָצוֹן מִלְּפָנֶיךָ יְהֹוָה אֱלֹהֵינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵינוּ... &#x05E2;&#x05D1;&#x05E8;&#x05D9;&#x05EA; &#x25BE;
Master of the Universe — what shall I say and what shall I speak? In everything that I begin to pray and to entreat before You — I immediately become confused and my mind is disturbed; and I do not know what to ask and what to request. For I have already fallen so very far down in all matters; and it is impossible to explain or to enumerate even the beginning of the beginning of my falls.

And therefore I have come before You: please grant me merit speedily to complete fear of Your majesty [yiras ha'romemut]; and to complete settled mind [yishuv ha'da'as]; and to complete and whole fear of You — with complete knowledge [da'as shalem] without any foolishness at all.
רִבּוֹנוֹ שֶׁל עוֹלָם, מָה אוֹמַר וּמָה אֲדַבֵּר... &#x05E2;&#x05D1;&#x05E8;&#x05D9;&#x05EA; &#x25BE;
Master of the Universe — awesome and terrible One: help me and save me and grant me merit speedily to the fear of majesty [yiras ha'romemut] — to know and to sense and to feel at every time and every moment that You are the King; the King of kings; the Holy One blessed be He; Whose glory fills the entire earth; Whose honor fills the entire universe; before Whom the heavenly host and the earthly host bow down. And help me and save me that I merit to arrive always at true and authentic prayer and at true conversation [sichas da'as] before You; in such a manner that all my prayers and conversations shall truly be a prayer for the Most High [tefillah l'El Elyon]. And help me and save me that I merit through this to draw down upon myself awesome and wonderful salvations from You always; and may I merit to draw down great salvation for the entire Jewish people; as it is written: With joy shall you draw water from the springs of salvation [Isaiah 12:3].

רִבּוֹנוֹ שֶׁל עוֹלָם, אָיוֹם וְנוֹרָא, עָזְרֵנִי וְהוֹשִׁיעֵנִי... &#x05E2;&#x05D1;&#x05E8;&#x05D9;&#x05ET; &#x25BE;
Master of the Universe — full of mercy; good and beneficent to all: grant me merit to taste the true taste of Shabbos delight [ta'am oneg Shabbos]; for You know how very far I am from this in truth. And have mercy upon me and help me and save me — that I merit to always receive the holy Shabbos with great holiness and purity; and may I merit through the holiness of the holy Shabbos to repair all my blemishes; as is well known to You. May the words of my mouth and the meditation of my heart be acceptable before You — Hashem, my Rock and my Redeemer [Psalms 19:15].
רִבּוֹנוֹ שֶׁל עוֹלָם, מָלֵא רַחֲמִים, טוֹב וּמֵטִיב לַכֹּל...
